 ## Background
-The method originates from the paper "3D Scene De-occlusion in Neural Radiance Fields: A Framework for Obstacle Removal and Realistic Inpainting" [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of applying 2D inpainting directly to NeRFs, which often results in 3D inconsistencies. The method was evaluated on datasets such as LLFF and SPIn-NeRF [S1].
+The method was proposed in the paper "3D Scene De-occlusion in Neural Radiance Fields: A Framework for Obstacle Removal and Realistic Inpainting" [S1]. It builds upon Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) [S1] and addresses the limitations of single 2D image inpainting in 3D scenes [S1]. The method has been evaluated on datasets including NeRF LLFF and SPIn-NeRF [S1].
 
